Feature: Pagination Consistency Across List Pages
  As a platform user (Editor, Admin, Advertiser)
  I want every list page to actually show all my data, not just a silently truncated first page
  So that I can find campaigns, assets, renders, and users beyond whatever the default page size happens to catch

  Background:
    Given I am logged in
    And the backend list endpoints (/api/campaigns, /api/assets, /api/renders, /api/users) support
      pagination via PaginationParams (page, pageSize, sortBy, sortDescending)

  Scenario: Assets view — Campaign Database grid is paginated
    Given more than 20 campaigns exist
    When I open the Assets view with no campaign selected
    Then the Campaign Database grid shows page 1 of the campaign list
    And pagination controls let me navigate to subsequent pages
    And a search box lets me filter by campaign name/code across all pages, not just the loaded ones

  Scenario: Assets view — Campaign Assets list is paginated
    Given a selected campaign has more than 20 assets
    When I view that campaign's asset manager
    Then the Campaign Assets list shows page 1 of that campaign's assets
    And pagination controls let me navigate to subsequent pages

  Scenario: Assets view — Unassigned Assets list is paginated
    Given more than 20 unassigned (no CampaignId) assets exist
    When I view the Assets staging area with no campaign selected
    Then the Unassigned Assets list shows page 1 of unassigned assets
    And pagination controls let me navigate to subsequent pages

  Scenario: Renders view is paginated and scoped to the selected campaign
    Given the selected campaign has more than 20 renders
    When I open the Renders tab
    Then the render queue shows page 1 of that campaign's renders
    And pagination controls let me navigate to subsequent pages
    And a status filter lets me narrow to Processing/Finished/Failed
    And the three summary stat cards (Processing/Completed/Failed) reflect the campaign's true totals, not just the current page

  Scenario: Admin → Users directory is paginated
    Given more than 20 users are registered
    When an Admin opens the Users directory
    Then the table shows page 1 of registered users
    And pagination controls let me navigate to subsequent pages
    And the search box queries the full user directory server-side, not just the loaded page
    And the role-breakdown stat cards (Admin/Editor/Advertiser) reflect true totals, not just the current page

  Scenario: Existing admin safety rules are unaffected by pagination
    Given the last remaining Admin account exists
    When another admin attempts to demote, suspend, or delete that account
    Then the operation is still blocked
    And this check uses the full unfiltered user set internally, not a paginated page

  Scenario: Global campaign picker (top-nav CampaignSelector) is a known, separate gap
    Given more than 20 campaigns exist
    When I open the top navigation bar's campaign switcher
    Then it still only searches within the first 20 campaigns loaded at app startup
    And this is intentionally out of scope for this fix — it requires reworking App.tsx's shared
      cross-page campaignList/assetList state, which many other views depend on for lookups
